    "Name": "Gerrida",
    "Details": "The C configuration of the Gerrida hovertank carries ten iATM-3 launchers in its turret, letting it harass enemies at extreme range or deal horrific damage at short range. Its ammunition bins hold standard, extended range, high explosive, inferno and EMP missiles, while a Nova CEWS handles electronic warfare. Being part of a Gerrida crew is a status symbol in the Society, and competition between vehicle crews for open spots is high.\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Biome Restrictions: None.</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Movement: 7/11 hexes / 210/330 meters.</color></b>\n\n<color=#ffcc00><b>Armor:</b> Ferro-Lamellor (C)\n<b>Structure:</b> Structure\n<b>Values       A        S  </b>\n<b>Front</b>       225     70\n<b>Left</b>         180     70\n<b>Right</b>       180     70\n<b>Rear</b>        150     70\n<b>Turret</b>      200     70\n\n<b>Total</b>      935    350</color>\n\n<color=#ff0000>Quirk: Distracting</color>\n\n<color=#ffcc00> Omni Vehicle</color>",
    "Icon": "Gerrida"
  },
  "YangsThoughts": "This one’s all about picking the right missile for the job. The iATMs can harass targets from way out or switch loads and absolutely tear them apart once the Gerrida closes the distance. With this thing’s speed, getting into the right range shouldn’t be much of a problem.",
